    relevance: "Permissions, protocol headers, capability sets, and option flags are all bit patterns. The mask idiom — test with &, set with |=, clear with &= ~, toggle with ^= — is one of C's most-used vocabularies, and it is exactly how Unix file permissions (rwx = 4/2/1) are stored.",
